From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:45:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/71] Log per-request token statistics so the cost mechanisms
 can be priced

Nine mechanisms trim what reaches the model and every one of them is
silent, so their savings have only ever been estimated from item sizes.
Each row pairs the provider's billed usage with the filtering report for
the prompt that produced it, which is enough to reconstruct the prompt an
unoptimised harness would have sent.

Rows go to a sidecar under the Codex home rather than into the rollout: a
new RolloutItem variant would reach the generated schemas, the TypeScript
bindings and the store migrations, and would make measurement part of the
resumable-session contract. The write happens where the provider's usage
lands, which covers ordinary turns, the memory refresh and compaction
without any of them knowing about it.

Off unless the request_stats feature is set, and nothing on the wire
changes: only the assembled Prompt is inspected, and only for counts.
